id: quick-draw
name: Quick Draw
kind: crafting
slots: 1
source: Core Rule
description: >
  Drawn: 1(T) on the Strike if your next Maneuver is an attack. Put away: 2(T) on the Wound of
  the next attack with it.
# What it does, for the Effects on its Item's sheet: its Effects line as printed, word for
# word, cut into one line to an effect, each opening with its tag as the rulebook writes one.
summary: >
  [Passive]: When you Unsheathe this Weapon, if your next Maneuver is an Attacking Maneuver,
  increase the Strike Roll of that Attacking Maneuver by 1(T). If you would Sheathe this Weapon,
  increase the Wound Roll of the next Attacking Maneuver you would make with this Weapon by
  2(T).
text: >
  Quick Draw: This Weapon is easy to ready, allowing you to attack with greater ease.
  –Weapon Type: All
  –Prerequisites: N/A
  –Quality Slots: 1
  –Effects: When you Unsheathe this Weapon, if your next Maneuver is an Attacking Maneuver,
  increase the Strike Roll of that Attacking Maneuver by 1(T). If you would Sheathe this Weapon,
  increase the Wound Roll of the next Attacking Maneuver you would make with this Weapon by
  2(T).

---

# Unsheathing is Wield, Sheathing is Sheathe, on the Weapon's row. Drawn, the next Maneuver takes
# the Strike's 1(T) if it is an attack - any other spends it. Put away, the Wound's 2(T) waits for
# the next attack made with it, whenever that is.
[passive]
weapon.quickDraw = true;
